[TEST] Urgent targeted neurologic examination:  
- Record Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) score (E/V/M);  
- Assess bilateral pupillary size and reactivity to light;  
- Test for nuchal rigidity (passive neck flexion);  
- Perform fundoscopic exam for papilledema;  
- Note any focal motor deficit or abnormal posturing.  
Please report all findings immediately.

